# Set what this box is, without a screen.
#
# To use it: make a file called "alnasl-mode.txt" in this folder whose FIRST
# line is one of the words below, and boot the Pi.
# This example does not count as it is: its first line is this comment.
#
#   alnasl  runs the hall: Alnasl and the hall screen (the default)
#   arkab   reads DGT boards and passes them to an Alnasl box
#   polis   the print station: prints what Alnasl sends to a printer on this box
#   nunki   the announcer: speaks the hall's announcements through HDMI or the
#           headphone jack
#   spare   an alnasl box that stands by: paired with a hall in the cloud, it
#           waits, and takes the hall over when the box running it goes silent
#           (or someone presses Take over). See alnasl-replica.txt.example too.
#
# v6's words still work: master means alnasl, slave means arkab.
# The file is read at boot and deleted. Nothing is erased: every role keeps its
# data, so switching back loses nothing. An Arkab box is joined to its Alnasl
# on its own status page (http://<this box>:4050), once it is on the network.
